Add public reset() method to MemorySpool.

MemorySpool (SingletonInterface) queues emails in memory, flushed
via __destruct() which fires only at process death. Under
long-running runtimes this means emails queue indefinitely and may
flush mid-way through an unrelated request.

Add a public reset() method to discard queued messages without
sending them, giving callers a controlled cleanup point.

--- a/Classes/Mail/MemorySpool.php
+++ b/Classes/Mail/MemorySpool.php
@@ -123,4 +123,15 @@
     {
         return 'MemorySpool';
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Discards all queued messages without sending them.
+     *
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where the singleton survives
+     * across requests and queued messages must not leak between requests.
+     */
+    public function reset(): void
+    {
+        $this->queuedMessages = [];
+    }
 }
